  "description": "A Monday-Friday story continues on Thursday (lacquer) and ends by alignment on Friday. Tuesday agreement entered later splits it: story-1 now ends on Tuesday, and the successor story-1+1 runs from Thursday to the Friday alignment. The backfilled write revises story-1's end act through the reconciliation story-1/v1 (@outcome revise, @basis the triggering record, no @frame), whose context is at the triggering record's occurrence time, and records the successor's begin act and its end act at the former ending. The split reconciliation and the successor's detection are generated as before; transition records are listed only in transition_acts. Each story read shows its own period, story-1's end with revised_by.",
